# Nothing regenerable is tracked. `make all` rebuilds this project end to end
# from the R scripts alone (~6 s, ~10 MB downloaded) — see R/00_prepare_data.R.

# Raw Météo-France source data — downloaded on demand by stage 00 from the
# mirror in R/config.R (MF_BASE_URL). Public, Licence Ouverte, no credentials.
# NOTE: the upstream filenames encode years and rotate each January; bump
#       MF_ERAS in R/config.R when the cycle turns.
data/raw/

# Moscow and Voronezh's raw data is a MANUAL export from Roshydromet's
# AISORI-M — login-gated, no stable URL, so unlike every other site `make
# all` cannot regenerate it. NOT committed anyway: its licence says personal,
# non-commercial use only, and redistributing the raw file goes beyond that.
# A fresh clone needs the export re-placed in data/raw/<site>/ by hand — see
# each site's "Why only one station?" note and R/sources/meteoru.R.

# Cached station extract + intermediates — regenerable via `make prepare`
data/processed/

# Generated analysis outputs — rebuilt by `make all` / `make all SITE=<site>`.
# Each report is the shareable artifact: copy it out, do not commit it (a
# multi-MB base64 HTML re-inflates the history on every refresh).
# EXCEPTION: every site's five PNG figures ARE tracked. README.md renders each
# site's report inline (see R/03_readme.R) and GitHub can only show the
# figures if they live in the repository. Figure refreshes are ordinary
# sequential commits (no amend/force-push) — see the climatudes-release-workflow
# memory. git requires each intermediate directory re-included explicitly,
# hence one block per site (castanet keeps its legacy root path).
outputs/*
!outputs/figures/
outputs/figures/*
!outputs/figures/*.png

!outputs/zurich/
outputs/zurich/*
!outputs/zurich/figures/
outputs/zurich/figures/*
!outputs/zurich/figures/*.png

